    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d339">

                <pb facs="0378" n="304" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg304"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 862.20261/28</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul at Tiflis</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 106</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 12, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department acknowledges the receipt of
                    your despatch of October 4, 1917, No. 66,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d339-f1"/> on the
                    subject of propaganda among the Kurdish tribes. As the purpose of your
                    suggestion appears to be the organization of an uprising against the Turks, with
                    whose Government the United States is not at war, it is not possible for the
                    Department to approve the interesting plan which you suggest.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilbur J. Carr</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
